 "notes": "C7 is judged raised. The referee says quadratic Ginzburg-Landau dependence cannot discriminate pairing symmetry; P8 says the anisotropic-pairing claim lacks an isotropic baseline. Both lead the authors to drop or justify the claim. P2 concerns the slope's robustness to the choice of data points, not the per-sample variation of the clean-limit term with d, so C2 is not raised. C1 is also absent from the review. C6 is not matched, because P8 asks for Lk(I) toward I* for pairing reasons, not as a DC cross-check of Lk. The supplement already gives a DC Ic of about 0.4 mA, but it does not extract Lk from it, so C6 is not fixed in v1. P3 is rated major because a constant contact or lead offset would bias all extracted Lk values, most strongly for the thick devices and the clean-limit intercept.",
